<DocsLayout title="Edit mode and authentication" description="Activate the editor through a same-origin v2 backend and choose built-in or host authentication.">
  <h1>Edit mode and authentication</h1>
  <p class="lead">Add <code>?copypatch=1</code> to an application page. CopyPatch then loads the editor client and calls the same-origin v2 route.</p>

  <h2>Authentication choices</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Strategy</th><th>Use when</th><th>Mutation protection</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>passphraseHash</code></td><td>You want CopyPatch-managed editor access.</td><td>Built-in secure same-site session, CSRF header, rate limit, and role checks.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>authAdapter</code></td><td>Your host already has accounts and access control.</td><td>The adapter verifies the host request and supplies roles for every mutation.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p>Both strategies use <code>editor</code> for draft changes and <code>publisher</code> for publication. They are mutually exclusive backend options.</p>

  <h2>Host-auth adapter responsibilities</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Resolve the authenticated host user into a principal with CopyPatch roles.</li>
    <li>Verify each mutating request with the host's CSRF or request-integrity mechanism.</li>
    <li>Pass a trusted client address through context when rate limiting needs it.</li>
  </ul>
</DocsLayout>
